# 3D coupled Level-Set / VOF (CLSVOF) and integral surface tension

This directory extends Basilisk's 2D CLSVOF and integral surface-tension
formulation (`two-phase-clsvof.h`, `two-phase-levelset.h`, and `integral.h`)
to 3D (while remaining backward-compatible with 1D, 2D, and axisymmetric
simulations).

## Usage

Include the headers from this sandbox (with `BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH`
pointing to `sandbox/`):

~~~literatec
#include "acastillo/clsvof/two-phase-clsvof.h"
#include "acastillo/clsvof/integral.h"
~~~

By default (`INTEGRAL_TENSOR=0`), constant surface tension uses the direct
3D line-integral formulation; compile with `-DINTEGRAL_TENSOR=1` to enable
the full $3\times 3$ capillary-stress tensor (supporting variable surface
tension / Marangoni flows in 2D, `AXI`, and 3D).

## Summary of changes vs. `$BASILISK/src/`

* [two-phase-clsvof.h](two-phase-clsvof.h): Extends vertex averaging of the
  signed distance `d` to 1D/2D/3D (8-cell average in 3D) and normalizes
  `plane_alpha(f[], n)` by $\|\mathbf{n}\|_2$ to obtain the Euclidean signed
  distance in all dimensions during VOF-to-levelset relaxation.
* [two-phase-levelset.h](two-phase-levelset.h): Extends `levelset_to_vof()`
  vertex averaging of `d` to 1D/2D/3D.
* [integral.h](integral.h): Extends the integral surface-tension formulation
  to 3D with:
  * **`INTEGRAL_TENSOR=0`**: Exact 3D triangulated face-intersection
    line integral for constant surface tension $\sigma$.
  * **`INTEGRAL_TENSOR=1`**: Full $3\times 3$ capillary-stress
    tensor $\mathbf{S}_h$ supporting spatially varying $\sigma$ (Marangoni
    stresses) in 2D, `AXI`, and 3D, with machine-zero force on tilted planes
    and machine-zero global momentum conservation.
  * Portable helper signatures (no helper-only `typedef struct`) so the
    operator also compiles cleanly on GPU/CUDA backends.
